// grmb design corpus. Hand-written against docs/design/grmb-spec.md (cycle 1
// grammar); NOT machine-checked (the P1 parser predates cycle 1). Findings below
// are what the rules of that file predict, to be confirmed by P0/P1.
// Stress 6: polling or pagination loop that is not a retry
//
// EXPECTED FINDINGS
//   retry would raise PLAN016 and mislead (success, not failure, repeats)
//   Workaround: a step `fetch_all` with an outcome { ok, partial }; the loop lives in code
// NOT EXPRESSIBLE (open questions: docs/design/grmb-spec.md 19)
//   loop over a success outcome with a data-dependent exit -- open question G2

step system.fetch_page : { ok, last_page };
scenario list realizes u.list_items {
  u.opens_list -> system.fetch_page => { ok => end ok; last_page => end ok; }
  // ok must repeat until last_page; retry is wrong (not a failure), no loop construct exists
}
